LICENSING EXCEPTION: LINUX eBPF PROBES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Components under the Linux eBPF probe directories are licensed under the
GNU General Public License, version 2 ("GPL-2.0"), and not under Apache-2.0.

This is a technical constraint, not a policy preference. The Linux kernel BPF
verifier restricts the majority of BPF helper functions -- including those this
project fundamentally requires -- to programs that declare a GPL-compatible
license in their `license` ELF section. A non-GPL eBPF probe would be rejected
at load time.

The exception is scoped as narrowly as possible: it covers only the eBPF
programs that execute inside the kernel. The userspace loader, the event
normalizer, and every other component of the agent remain Apache-2.0.

Each affected source file carries its own SPDX identifier. The SPDX identifier
in a file is authoritative for that file.

